+- A red commit that a CI test wraps (for example a dotnet test that runs a python test) turns main's CI red by construction (card 266, 2026-11-07: the CI run on the red-2 commit failed); it is pushed together with its green, not alone.
@@ -518,0 +520,6 @@
+- **Guard tests read committed blobs (experiment).** A test that guards a card's own change by comparing history or bytes (a byte-parity test, a byte-rule test, an untouched-files test) reads committed blobs (`git show <sha>:path`), never the working tree, and selects its commit by a hash recorded in the card's record or by an exact subject, never by a subject prefix; it carries one red that adds a later look-alike commit and an uncommitted edit and must stay green. A mutation patch is run and shown failing before it is filed, and its file name says what it does (it applies forward). A guard on live state (a scan that old names stay out of the live docs) reads the working tree on purpose.
+  - Hypothesis: guards that read committed blobs and select by exact key stay valid after later record commits, so they are not found broken at review. Metric: guard-test defects found at review or sign-off per card that adds guard tests (card 266: 2, the byte-rule tests reading the working tree and two mislabelled mutation patches), target 0. Counter-metric: guard-authoring minutes (under 10 per test) and extra red rewrites from selector brittleness. Trial: the next 3 cards that add guard tests. Decider D206, started 2026-11-07.
+
+- **A cold-reader seat and the story-promise check for docs cards (experiment).** A card whose story promises something about what a reader finds (a README, a guide, the docs) gets a cold-reader seat at the gate: a fresh model reads only the named docs as the story's persona with no other context and reports what is wrong, confusing or fine to leave, by file and line; and at Ready the card's criteria are checked against the story's promise: a promise the criteria do not cover is added to the criteria or filed as a new card. The seat may not edit and runs nothing.
+  - Hypothesis: a fresh reader plus a Ready-time promise check finds the gap between a docs story and its criteria before sign-off, not after. Metric: story promises not covered by the criteria and found only at the gate or sign-off per docs card (card 266: 1, the stale status and Layout text), target 0 found late. Counter-metric: cold-reader minutes (card 266: under 1) and findings the card cannot act on. Trial: the next 3 docs cards. Decider D206, started 2026-11-07.
